<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Spanish trawler reported taking water off Ireland.</title>
<headline>Spanish trawler reported taking water off Ireland.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1996-10-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 15-member crew of a Spanish fishing trawler were trying to keep their vessel afloat on Saturday after it started taking water in the Atlantic off the southwest coast of Ireland.</p>
<p>The captain of the Eclipse 2 told Irish coastguards his vessel would sink in four to six hours unless the water could be pumped out.</p>
<p>Irish coastguards said a helicopter carrying a pump was on its way to the trawler, which was about 160 miles from land. The weather was good and there were no immediate plans to evacuate the crew, a spokesman added.</p>
</text>
